# ===========================================================================
#  Computational package for
#  "Net electron spin rotation in a plane-wave pulse:
#   Holonomy set by the anomalous magnetic moment"
#
#  READ BEFORE CHANGING
#  --------------------
#  MANIFEST.sha256 records the SHA-256 digest of every deposited file byte for
#  byte, and `python reproduce_all.py --verify` checks a copy against it.  The
#  files keep the line endings they were written with: most results and
#  several sources were written on Windows (CRLF), the rest have LF.  The
#  results are byte-identical to those of deposit v1.0.1.
#
#  If git were allowed to convert line endings (core.autocrlf, text=auto,
#  eol=...), a clone would hold different bytes from the deposit on some
#  platforms, and --verify would fail although no number had changed.  The
#  rule below turns every conversion off, whatever the settings of the person
#  cloning: git stores and checks out each file exactly as deposited.
#
#  Do not add text, eol or text=auto rules.  To change the line endings of a
#  file on purpose, change the file itself, then run
#  `python reproduce_all.py --manifest`.
# ===========================================================================

# No line-ending conversion, for any file.
*        -text

# Images and documents: also no textual diff or merge.
*.png    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.eps    binary
